    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d993">

                <pb facs="1153" n="957" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg957"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/7–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 993<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied
                        Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d993-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-25">July 25, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 286. From Ambassador E. W. Pauley
                    Tripartite Conference <hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 286 to American
                    Legation Stockholm: information to AmLegations [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >sic</hi>] Paris, London, Lisbon, Madrid, Bern, AGWar for SecState.</p>
                <p>There is presently under consideration at Berlin Conference proposal for
                    declaration of power over German external assets, whose issuance in near future
                    however seems doubtful. Reurtel giving reaction Rubin’s telegram July 19.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d993-f2"/> Draft decree vesting in agency operating within
                    framework of ACC all right, title and interest in German external assets also
                    under consideration.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d993-f3"/> As decree now stands it
                    would automatically vest such interest, and would be exercise of its power to
                    vest by ACC. Text of proposed decree being sent Legation by pouch. Proposed to
                    turn decree over to US Group CC for consideration and presentation to other ACC
                    members.</p>
                <pb facs="1154" n="958" xml:id="pg958"/>
                <p>Necessity for some formal action establishing right of Allied governments to
                    supervise and control important German external properties, especially in
                    countries like Spain, Portugal and Switzerland, makes exercise of vesting power
                    desirable.</p>
                <p>This telegram cleared with Clayton.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
